<BaseLayout title="About | SilverBack Barbell Club" description="Training for adults who want strength, resilience, and longevity without fitness-industry noise." canonicalPath="/about/">
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="site-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">What the club is</p>
      <h1>Training that still makes sense years from now.</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>SilverBack Barbell Club is for adults who have trained long enough to know that consistency matters more than spectacle. The sessions build useful strength, joint confidence, balance, power, and work capacity without turning every day into a test.</p>
        <h2>Who it is for</h2>
        <p>People who want to train hard and keep training. Experience helps, but the work is written to scale to the person in front of it. Readiness, range, and load are decisions made in the gym.</p>
        <h2>How we train</h2>
        <p>Every session starts by preparing the positions it asks you to use and ends with a deliberate warm-down. Between those points, the structure follows the day’s objective. Some days are heavy. Some are athletic. Some are steady. None need novelty for novelty’s sake.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
